  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Elevated fire weather conditions (hot, dry, breezy) lasting \n   into the weekend region-wide.\n\n-  Wildfire smoke degrading air quality and reducing visibility\n   for the next several days and likely well into next week.\n\nOverview of the coming week demonstrates a drier less convective\nsouthwest flow will develop. Additionally, regional smoke is\nlikely to add stability to the atmosphere. \n\nNear term: Elevated fire weather concerns throughout this weekend\nwill be present. Hot, dry, and windy conditions will be prevalent.\nCaution should be used on area lakes as choppy conditions are \nexpected. \n\nScattered thunderstorms are possible this evening from Lost Trail\nPass through Butte and Deer Lodge. With lower levels of the\natmosphere so dry, gusty outflow winds 40 to 50 mph will be\npossible. \n\nRegional smoke will also continue to move into the Northern\nRockies with southwest flow. High resolution models do not depict\na significant worsening in air quality or improvement in the short\nterm. The caveat would be any new local fires causing degradations\nto isolated areas. \n\nThe upper level pattern changes very little for early next week,\nwith hot, dry and smoky conditions continuing. Monsoonal moisture\nwill remain predominantly suppressed to the south, limiting \nthunderstorm potential to occasional, slight chances across Lemhi \nCounty and southwest Montana. Forecast models do hint at high \npressure restrengthening over the area by Thursday/ Friday, which\nwould allow for further warming of temperatures and possibly for \nthicker smoke to settle into valley bottoms.",
